WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you, Colton?
-Good, man. How you doing?

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.772
Good. We´ve known each other
for years and years and years.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:06.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-2001, I believe.
-2001.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met in Amsterdam.
-That´s right.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:10.543 size:84% position:42%
-Because we both worked
for a comedy theater

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.811 size:75% position:38%
called Boom Chicago.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s right, Boom Chicago.
-A fantastic place.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.849 size:81% position:41%
A lot of our friends
got their start there.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was there before you.
-Yeah.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You came after me.
Did you find --

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.222
I found a little bit of culture
shock when I moved to Amsterdam.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah?
-How was it for you?

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I found a lot.
A lot of culture shock, yeah.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was most shocking to you
culturally?

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Let´s see.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:34.067
Well, probably the most shocking
part of living in Holland is

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
they celebrate the holidays
a little differently.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They start a little earlier.
You know?

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, for them,
Christmas kind of starts

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
around the second week of
December.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everybody starts putting up
their decorations

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.379
and having a lot of fun, right?

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I´m riding into work
on a bike,

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of course
everybody rides bikes.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.820
-And where we worked, it was
still also a neighborhood,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
so there´s little kids
going to school

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.489
same time I´m riding to work.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:00.393
But on this day in the holidays
the kids all have black face on.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, like black face.
-This is a real thing.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, hey --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.869
"I´m a little kid, you know."

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was weird.
-Yeah.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then they saw me
and they´d go --

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.942
[ Speaking foreign language ]

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:18.111
Which means "black Pete."

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were really happy
about it.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. They were happy
to see black Pete.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:26.519
-Yeah, see, ´cause the thing is,
is that in Holland Santa Claus,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:30.156
he doesn´t have little elves
that help him deliver toys.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has straight-up slaves.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:37.197
And they portray those slaves
by having white Dutch people

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
put on black face
and run around.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the story goes
if you´re a bad kid,

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:46.106
these slaves will throw you in a
sack and take you back to Spain.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.476 size:78% position:39%
-It´s a bummer story.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:53.646
-It´s a bummer story all around,
especially for the slaves.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:58.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so what did you say
to the children

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
who were saying black Pete
to you?

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn´t say much.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
I fought them.
All of them.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:04.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.025
All of Holland´s children.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember
you did a sketch as a --

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did.
Actually, me and Jordan Peele.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Jordan Peele
from "Key &amp; Peele."

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys played a couple of
aggressive black Petes.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.770
-And it was a fantastic sketch.
And I think that --

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:21.674
-That´s how we fought back.
We fought back with a rap song.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.276
-So you met Jordan out there.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:24.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-Jordan Peele.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you wrote for
"Key &amp; Peele."

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.748
And Jordan, who wrote and
directed the film, "Get Out" --

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.016 size:88% position:44%
a fantastic horror film.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s right.
Did you guys see that?

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wow.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:34.687 size:84% position:42%
-He -- Do you remember?

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because he had that idea
for years.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember the first time
he told you about it?

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.326
-Oh, yeah. I remember the first
time he told it to me.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.862
And, you know, spoiler alert --

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
has something to do
with black people

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:48.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting their head cut off.
And I was like, "What?

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re going to make
a whole movie about it?"

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:54.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was like, "Yeah, man,
I think I´m going do it."

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he did it!
-He did it.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he nailed it.
-He fully nailed it.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He nailed it.

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:02.582
-So you guys -- So then you went
and you wrote for "Key &amp; Peele."

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And were there any sketches
that sort of --

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.789
that you worked on that came out
of sort of working with people

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.257
you´ve known for a long time?

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. The best thing about
working on a show

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
like "Key &amp; Peele,"
we were all just friends.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:17.564
And so a lot of sketches just
came out of kind of hanging out.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know how that is sort of
in the sketch room.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:22.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, one time I showed up
to a meeting,

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:25.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was no more chair
for me to sit in.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.807 size:81% position:41%
And so I just kind of
leaned on this cabinet

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.475
that was not very steady.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.044
And I´m not a little guy,

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:34.614
